streaming-gltf ModelPool (examples/local-progressive/model-pool.js) decodes baked KHR_texture_basisu (KTX2) textures via KTX2Loader.setTranscoderPath(new URL('./basis/', import.meta.url)), expecting examples/local-progressive/basis/basis_transcoder.{js,wasm}. But the package.json `files` field is ["index.js","examples/local-progressive/*.js","tools/*.mjs",...] — the glob *.js does NOT match the basis/ SUBDIR, so the published npm package OMITS the basis transcoder. Result: on any static host (gh-pages) the transcoder 404s and the whole .prog-routed map renders UNTEXTURED (witnessed tex 1/101 meshes on the deployed spoint demo). spoint's WORKAROUND: gh-pages.yml stages client/basis/basis_transcoder.{js,wasm} into dist/node_modules/streaming-gltf/examples/local-progressive/basis/ after copying the pkg (deployed tex -> 97/101). PROPER upstream fix: add 'examples/local-progressive/basis/*' (and any wasm assets) to streaming-gltf package.json files, bump, republish, then spoint consumes it and the gh-pages staging can be dropped. NOTE dev copy C:/dev/streaming-gltf was at 1.0.18 while spoint consumed published 1.0.19 — do not publish from the stale dev tree without syncing first. Local spoint dev does NOT hit this because no .prog is baked on disk so models use the legacy EntityLoader path (original textures); only the prebaked-.prog deploy routes through ModelPool+KTX2.